Force the apple_support exec-tool linker (wrapped_clang / wrapped_clang_pp /
libtool) to emit an LC_UUID load command.

Xcode 26's linker (ld-prime) can produce these universal exec tools without an
LC_UUID, and macOS 26's dyld refuses to load a Mach-O that has no LC_UUID
("missing LC_UUID load command"), which breaks every C/C++ compile action.
Passing -Wl,-random_uuid makes ld always write a UUID.

--- a/crosstool/universal_exec_tool.bzl
+++ b/crosstool/universal_exec_tool.bzl
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
     -arch arm64 \
     -arch x86_64 \
     -O3 \
+    -Wl,-random_uuid \
     -o $@ \
     $(SRCS)
 """,
